==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*2 [[Zroco]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*2 [[Zroco]]s spawn after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*2 [[Zroco]]s spawn after 166.67 seconds<sup>5,000f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Zamelle]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Oldhorn]]s spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Use Anti-Relic Crowd-Controllers like [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]]. Use [[Delinquent Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ultra Delinquent Cat]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]], and/or [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]] to subdue the Oldhorns, and use [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]] like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] to chip down Zamelle, or even some Long Distance units. The Zrocos are easily killed with by [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|Anti-Zombie]]/[[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer]] Units, such as [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cat]], [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]], or [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]].

If one owns the elusive [[Brainwashed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Fish Cat]], it can be of great help, being a general stat-stick VS the Doge Dark or Oldhorn, and helping whittle down Zamelle during cleanup.

If one has talented [[Detective Vigler (Uber Rare Cat)]] then this stage becomes much easier.

